# Secrets — never commit.
#
# Matched by prefix, not by exact name: a backup, a dated copy, or a
# `.env.bak` written in a hurry carries exactly the same credentials as `.env`
# itself, and an exact-match rule silently lets every one of them through.
# Two branches hit this independently, each committing a pre-edit backup of
# `.env` locally and catching it before it reached the remote, so the rule is
# deliberately wider than either incident needed. `.env*` also covers bare
# `.env`, which a `.env.*` rule does not.
.env*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# The database lives at ~/.org/org.db, outside this repo by design.
# These patterns are belt-and-braces in case anyone points DB_PATH here.
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Financial exports dropped in for import
/statements/
*.ofx
*.qfx

# Dependencies & build output
node_modules/
dist/
build/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Python sidecar (services/quant). uv.lock IS committed — it pins the
# training environment, which has to be reproducible on another machine.
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Editors & OS
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json

# Logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
logs/

# Machine-local Claude Code permission grants
.claude/settings.local.json


# Kept out of iCloud Drive sync — this repo lives under a synced Desktop,
# and iCloud uploading ~60k build files corrupted node_modules, blocked
# every Node and Python process on file I/O, and left the server unable
# to restart. iCloud skips any path ending in .nosync; the real
# directories carry that suffix and are symlinked back to their normal
# names, so tooling sees no difference.
*.nosync
